# Dillon OS writing rules

Full source of truth: `System/writing-rules.md`. These apply to ALL client-facing output: emails, blog posts, social copy, reports, ad copy.

1. No em dashes anywhere. Ever. Use periods, commas, colons, or restructure.
2. Never start sentences with: And, But, Or, It is, Do not, That is, This is.
3. Always use contractions (don't, can't, won't, isn't).
4. In client-facing copy, use the bullet character (•) as the list marker, never dashes.
5. Conversational but professional. No corporate jargon, no AI-sounding language.
6. Client emails go out under Momentum 360 branding, never Buzz Bull.
7. Align HCM is NOT a Momentum 360 client. Never route Align HCM content under Momentum 360 branding.

